# Test tenant (production) — do not create another

`kame-test-tenant` (`org`), `kame-test-property`, `kame-test-parking` exist in production on
purpose, so an agent can measure and verify against real data without touching a host's rows.
It is **not a bug** and must not be removed.

Full reference: **`docs/architecture/test-tenant.md`**.

## Hard rules

| Rule                                                             | Why                                                                                                                                            |
| ---------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Never create a second test org.**                              | `organizations_single_test_tenant` is a unique index; the insert fails anyway, and a "workaround" would mean weakening a production guardrail. |
| **Never set `properties.is_test` / `parkings.is_test` by hand.** | A trigger derives them from the org. Writing them is ignored at best.                                                                          |
| **Never make a test listing `ACTIVE`.**                          | `properties_test_never_active` rejects it, and ACTIVE is exactly what would put it on public listing pages, search, facets and map results.    |
| **Never retype `organizations.is_test`.**                        | It is immutable by trigger; children would desynchronise.                                                                                      |
| **Never use the probe account on real tenants.**                 | It exists to read and measure the test org. Real hosts' data is off limits.                                                                    |
| **Never propose deleting the test tenant as cleanup.**           | It is intentional infrastructure. Say so if a lint or audit flags it.                                                                          |

## When you need somewhere to try something

1. Prefer the **local seed dataset** (`docs/guides/testing/local-seed-data.md`). Most work
   needs no production at all.
2. If it must be production (real edge latency, real caches, deployed build), use the existing
   test tenant read-only.
3. If the existing tenant genuinely cannot express the case, that is a **design decision**,
   not a quick insert. Write it down, get it reviewed, and change
   `docs/architecture/test-tenant.md` in the same change.

## Operating it

```bash
node scripts/dev/test-tenant.mjs            # read-only audit
CONFIRM_TEST_TENANT=yes node scripts/dev/test-tenant.mjs --apply   # create, once
```
